reports.definition_of_done:
The workstream has no spec and no end state of its own. The nearest stated goals:
(1) The roadmap in card #755: five ordered PRs, each closed by a card with its own acceptance criteria. The cards are #755, #768, #770, #772 and #779.
(2) Phase F's exit criteria, from the newest stored handoff: phase E's, `git show origin/claude/budgeted-autonomy-workspace:_handoff/budgeted-autonomy/handoff.md`, §4 lines 291-296. They are:
- the live run is recorded in the ledger and in the handoff;
- its findings are fixed and merged;
- #779 is closed with a `done` that names the evidence;
- every drift ask that was posted is answered;
- open questions 2 to 5 have been asked.
(3) Step 7 of the same handoff: run `/handoff budgeted-autonomy F`, and if the roadmap is closed, say so along with what remains queued.
(4) The decisions-log row of 2026-10-13 (tools/autonomy-controller/README.md:844): "#779 closes once the live run's follow-up PR merges".
The original brief is #755's Context paragraph: take an eligible card, claim it on the bus, implement it through a CLI, validate it in the devtest container, handle bounded PR revisions, merge through the permitted workflow, keep an audit record, start the next task fresh, and stop spending when the allowance is exhausted. Against that brief, the end state is partly undefined. No card covers the brief items that remain unbuilt.

